1
00:00:01,461 --> 00:00:13,904
(Q31) In today's class I'm going to talk about marine archaeology, the branch of archaeology focusing on human interaction with the sea, lakes and rivers. 今天的课程中，我将讨论海洋考古学，即研究人类与海洋、湖泊以及河流之间互动的考古学分支。⭐ marine archaeology = 海洋考古学（C1）｜the branch of... = ……的分支领域（C1）｜focus on human interaction with... = 关注人类与……之间的互动（C1）

2
00:00:13,904 --> 00:00:22,377
It's the study of ships, cargoes, shipping facilities, and other physical remains. 它研究船只、货物、航运设施以及其他实体遗迹。⭐ physical remains = 实物遗存；遗迹（C1）｜cargo = 货物（B2）

3
00:00:22,377 --> 00:00:32,372
I'll give you an example, then go on to show how this type of research is being transformed by the use of the latest technology. 我会先给大家一个例子，然后继续展示这种研究方式如何因最新技术的应用而发生改变。⭐ go on to do sth = 继续做某事（B2）｜be transformed by... = 被……改变/转变（C1）｜the use of the latest technology = 最新技术的应用（B2）

4
00:00:32,372 --> 00:00:44,092
Atlit-Yam was a village on the coast of the eastern Mediterranean, which seems to have been thriving until around 7,000 BC.&nbsp; <span style="color: oklch(0.278 0.033 256.848);">Atlit-Yam</span>是东地中海沿岸的一个村庄，似乎一直繁荣发展到公元前约7000年。 ⭐ on the coast of... = 位于……海岸（B2）｜thrive = 繁荣发展；兴旺（C1）

5
00:00:44,092 --> 00:00:59,969
The residents kept cattle, caught fish and stored grain. They had wells for fresh water, many of their houses were built around a courtyard and were constructed of stone. 居民饲养牛群、捕鱼并储存谷物。他们拥有获取淡水的水井，许多房屋围绕庭院建造，并由石头构成。⭐ keep cattle = 饲养牛群（B2）｜store grain = 储存谷物（B2）｜be constructed of... = 由……建造（B2）

6
00:00:59,969 --> 00:01:13,907
[Q31答案句] The village contained an impressive monument: seven half-tonne stones standing in a semicircle around a spring, that might have been used for ceremonial purposes. 这个村庄有一座令人印象深刻的纪念建筑：七块半吨重的石头围绕泉水呈半圆形排列，可能曾用于仪式用途。⭐ impressive monument = 令人印象深刻的遗迹/纪念建筑（C1）｜stand in a semicircle = 呈半圆形排列（C1）｜ceremonial purposes = 仪式用途（C1）

7
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:28,326
(Q32) Atlit-Yam may have been destroyed swiftly by a tsunami, or climate change may have caused glaciers to melt and sea levels to rise, flooding the village gradually.&nbsp; <span style="color: oklch(0.278 0.033 256.848);">Atlit-Yam</span>可能迅速被海啸摧毁，或者气候变化导致冰川融化、海平面上升，逐渐淹没了村庄。 ⭐ be destroyed by... = 被……摧毁（B2）｜cause sth to do sth = 导致某物发生某事（B2）｜sea levels rise = 海平面上升（B2）｜flood sth gradually = 逐渐淹没某物（C1）

8
00:01:28,326 --> 00:01:38,311
Whatever the cause, it now lies ten metres below the surface of the Mediterranean, buried under sand at the bottom of the sea. 无论原因是什么，如今它位于地中海海面以下10米处，被埋在海底的沙层之下。⭐ whatever the cause = 无论原因是什么（C1）｜lie below the surface = 位于表面以下（C1）｜be buried under... = 被埋在……之下（B2）

9
00:01:38,311 --> 00:01:47,628
It's been described as the largest and best preserved prehistoric settlement ever found on the seabed. 它被称为在海床上发现的规模最大、保存最完好的史前聚落。⭐ be described as... = 被描述为……（B2）｜well preserved = 保存完好的（B2）｜prehistoric settlement = 史前聚落（C1）｜seabed = 海床（C1）

10
00:01:47,628 --> 00:01:52,756
For marine archaeologists, Atlit-Yam is a treasure trove. 对于海洋考古学家来说，Atlit-Yam 是一座宝藏。⭐ treasure trove = 宝库；丰富来源（C1）

11
00:01:52,756 --> 00:02:05,703
[Q32答案句] Research on the buildings, tools and the human remains has revealed how the bustling village once functioned, and even what diseases some of its residents suffered from. 对建筑、工具以及人类遗骸的研究揭示了这个繁忙村庄曾经如何运作，甚至发现了一些居民患有的疾病。⭐ human remains = 人类遗骸（C1）｜reveal how... = 揭示……如何（B2）｜bustling = 繁忙的；热闹的（C1）｜suffer from... = 患有；遭受（B2）

12
00:02:05,703 --> 00:02:13,878
(Q33) But of course this is only one small village, one window into a lost world. 但当然，这只是一个小村庄，只是窥见失落世界的一扇窗口。⭐ a window into... = 了解……的窗口（C1）｜lost world = 消失的世界（B2）

13
00:02:13,878 --> 00:02:22,652
For a fuller picture, researchers need more sunken settlements, but the hard part is finding them. 为了获得更完整的图景，研究人员需要发现更多沉没的聚落，但困难之处在于找到它们。⭐ a fuller picture = 更完整的了解（C1）｜sunken settlement = 沉没的聚落（C1）｜the hard part is... = 难点在于……（B2）

14
00:02:22,652 --> 00:02:45,821
Underwater research used to require divers to find shipwrecks or artefacts, but in the second half of the twentieth century, various types of underwater vehicles were developed, some controlled from a ship on the surface, and some of them autonomous, which means they don't need to be operated by a person. 过去，水下研究需要潜水员寻找沉船或人工制品，但在20世纪后半叶，各种水下设备被开发出来，其中一些由水面船只控制，另一些则是自主运行的，也就是说不需要人工操作。⭐ used to do sth = 过去常常做某事（B2）｜shipwreck = 沉船（C1）｜artefact = 人工制品；文物（C1）｜autonomous = 自主的（C1）｜be operated by... = 由……操作（B2）

15
00:02:45,821 --> 00:03:00,638
[Q33答案句] Autonomous underwater vehicles, or AUVs, are used in the oil industry, for instance, to create maps of the seabed before rigs and pipelines are installed. 例如，自主水下航行器（AUV）被用于石油行业，在安装钻井设备和管道之前绘制海床地图。⭐ for instance = 例如（B2）｜create maps of... = 绘制……地图（B2）｜install pipelines = 安装管道（C1）

16
00:03:00,638 --> 00:03:17,198
(Q34) [Q34答案句] To navigate they use sensors such as compasses and sonar. Until relatively recently they were very expensive, and so heavy that they had to be launched from a large vessel with a winch. 为了导航，它们使用指南针和声呐等传感器。直到相对较近的时期，它们仍然非常昂贵，而且重量太大，只能通过大型船只上的绞车发射。⭐ navigate = 导航；定位（C1）｜sensor = 传感器（B2）｜until relatively recently = 直到最近一段时间（C1）｜so...that... = 如此……以至于……（B2）｜launch from... = 从……发射（B2）

17
00:03:17,198 --> 00:03:32,806
(Q35) But the latest AUVs are much easier to manoeuvre - they can be launched from the shore or a small ship. And they're much cheaper, which makes them more accessible to research teams. 但最新型的AUV更容易操控——它们可以从岸边或小船上发射。而且它们价格更低，使研究团队更容易使用。⭐ manoeuvre = 操控；操纵（C1）｜make sth accessible to... = 使某物更容易被……使用（C1）

18
00:03:32,806 --> 00:03:48,853
They're also very sophisticated. They can communicate with each other and, for example, work out the most efficient way to survey a site, or to find particular objects on the seabed. 它们也非常先进。它们可以相互通信，例如计算出调查某个地点或寻找海床中特定物体的最高效方式。⭐ sophisticated = 复杂先进的（C1）｜communicate with each other = 相互交流（B2）｜work out = 找出；计算出（B2）｜survey a site = 勘察地点（C1）

19
00:03:48,853 --> 00:03:52,657
Field tests show the approach can work. 实地测试表明，这种方法可行。⭐ field test = 实地测试（C1）｜the approach can work = 这种方法可行（B2）

20
00:03:52,657 --> 00:04:02,159
For example, in a trial in 2015, three AUVs searched for wrecks at Marzamemi, off the coast of Sicily. 例如，在2015年的一次测试中，三台自主水下航行器（AUV）在西西里岛海岸附近的 Marzamemi 寻找沉船。⭐ in a trial = 在一次试验/测试中（B2）｜search for = 寻找（B1，但在学术语境中常见）｜wreck = 沉船；失事船只（C1）｜off the coast of... = 在……海岸附近（B2）

21
00:04:02,159 --> 00:04:17,061
[Q35答案句] The site is the final resting place of an ancient Roman ship, which sank in the sixth century AD while ferrying prefabricated marble elements for the construction of an early church. 该地点是一艘古罗马船只的最终归宿。这艘船在公元6世纪沉没，当时正在运输用于建造早期教堂的预制大理石部件。⭐ final resting place = 最终归宿；安息之地（C1）｜sink = 沉没（B2）｜ferry sth = 运输某物（C1）｜prefabricated = 预制的（C1）

22
00:04:17,061 --> 00:04:25,319
(Q36) The AUVs mapped the area in detail, finding other ships carrying columns of the same material.&nbsp; AUV详细绘制了该区域地图，并发现了其他装载同种材料柱子的船只。 ⭐ map an area in detail = 详细绘制区域地图（C1）｜carry columns = 携带柱子（B2）

23
00:04:25,319 --> 00:04:33,128
Creating an internet in the sea for AUVs to communicate is no easy matter. 为AUV创造一个能够在海洋中通信的互联网并非易事。⭐ be no easy matter = 并非易事（C1）

24
00:04:33,128 --> 00:04:43,105
Wifi networks on land use electromagnetic waves, but in water these will only travel a few centimetres. 陆地上的WiFi网络使用电磁波，但在水中这些电磁波只能传播几厘米。⭐ electromagnetic waves = 电磁波（C1）｜travel a distance = 传播一段距离（B2）

25
00:04:43,105 --> 00:04:48,778
Instead, a more complex mix of technologies is required. 相反，这需要更加复杂的技术组合。⭐ a mix of technologies = 技术组合（C1）｜be required = 被需要（B2）

26
00:04:48,778 --> 00:04:59,801
[Q36答案句] For short distances, AUVs can share data using light while acoustic waves are used to communicate over long distances. 在短距离内，AUV可以利用光共享数据，而声波则用于远距离通信。⭐ share data = 共享数据（B2）｜acoustic waves = 声波（C1）｜over long distances = 长距离范围内（B2）

27
00:04:59,801 --> 00:05:18,987
(Q37) But more creative solutions are also being developed, where an AUV working on the seabed offloads data to a second AUV, which then surfaces and beams the data home to the research team using a satellite. 不过，更具创造性的解决方案也正在开发中：一台在海床工作的AUV将数据传输给另一台AUV，后者随后浮出水面，并通过卫星将数据发送回研究团队。⭐ creative solution = 创新解决方案（B2）｜offload data to... = 将数据转移给……（C1）｜surface = 浮出水面（C1）｜beam data = 发送数据（C1）

28
00:05:18,987 --> 00:05:27,979
There's also a system that enables AUVs to share information from seabed scans, and other data. 此外，还有一种系统能够让AUV共享来自海床扫描的信息以及其他数据。⭐ enable sb to do sth = 使某人能够做某事（B2）｜seabed scans = 海床扫描（C1）

29
00:05:27,979 --> 00:05:51,050
[Q37答案句] So if an AUV surveying the seabed finds an intriguing object, it can share the coordinates of the object - that is, its position - with a nearby AUV that carries superior cameras, and arrange for that AUV to make a closer inspection of the object. 因此，如果一台正在调查海床的AUV发现了一个有趣的物体，它可以将该物体的坐标（即位置）分享给附近配备更高级摄像头的AUV，并安排后者对该物体进行更近距离的检查。⭐ intriguing = 引人关注的；有趣的（C1）｜coordinates = 坐标（C1）｜make a closer inspection of... = 对……进行进一步检查（C1）

30
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:58,698
(Q38) Marine archaeologists are excited about the huge potential of these AUVs for their discipline. 海洋考古学家对这些AUV在他们领域中的巨大潜力感到兴奋。⭐ be excited about the potential of... = 对……潜力感到兴奋（C1）｜discipline = 学科；领域（C1）

31
00:05:58,698 --> 00:06:06,606
One site where they're going to be deployed is the Gulf of Baratti, off the Italian coast. 其中一个即将部署这些设备的地点是意大利海岸附近的巴拉蒂湾。⭐ be deployed = 被部署；投入使用（C1）｜off the coast of... = 在……海岸附近（B2）

32
00:06:06,606 --> 00:06:15,717
In 1974, a 2,000-year-old Roman vessel was discovered here, in 18 metres of water.&nbsp; <span style="color: oklch(0.278 0.033 256.848);">1974年，一艘有2000年历史的古罗马船只在这里被发现，位于水下18米处。</span> ⭐ <span style="color: oklch(0.278 0.033 256.848);">a 2,000-year-old + noun = 有2000年历史的……（B2）｜vessel = 船；舰艇（C1）｜be discovered = 被发现（B2）｜in ... metres of water = 位于水下……米处（C1）</span>

33
00:06:15,717 --> 00:06:24,372
[Q38答案句] When it sank, it was carrying medical goods, in wooden or tin receptacles. 沉没时，它载有装在木制或锡制容器中的医疗用品。⭐ medical goods = 医疗用品（B2）｜receptacle = 容器（C1）

34
00:06:24,372 --> 00:06:37,823
(Q39) [Q39答案句] Its cargo gives us insight into the treatments available all those years ago, including tablets that are thought to have been dissolved to form a cleansing liquid for the eyes. 它的货物让我们了解到几千年前可用的治疗方式，包括被认为溶解后用于制作眼部清洁液的药片。⭐ give insight into... = 使人深入了解……（C1）｜treatment available = 可用的治疗方法（B2）｜be thought to have done sth = 被认为曾做过某事（C1）｜dissolve = 溶解（B2）

35
00:06:37,823 --> 00:06:44,656
(Q40) Other Roman ships went down nearby, taking their cargoes with them. 附近还有其他罗马船只沉没，并带着它们的货物一起沉入海底。⭐ go down = 下沉；沉没（B2）｜take sth with them = 带着某物一起（B2）

36
00:06:44,656 --> 00:06:55,297
[Q40答案句] Some held huge pots made of terracotta. Some were used for transporting cargoes of olive oil, and others held wine. 一些船装有巨大的陶罐。一些陶罐用于运输橄榄油，另一些则装载葡萄酒。⭐ be made of... = 由……制成（B2）｜transport cargo = 运输货物（B2）

37
00:06:55,297 --> 00:06:57,797
In many cases it's only these containers that remain, while the wooden ships have been buried under silt on the seabed. 在很多情况下，留下来的只有这些容器，而木制船只已经被埋在海床的淤泥之下。⭐ in many cases = 在很多情况下（B2）｜remain = 留存（B2）｜be buried under... = 被埋在……下面（B2）｜silt = 淤泥（C1）

